<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:52Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>India news: New Delhi denies claims world leaders fell ill after BRICS summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e01ec27a80bd8fc22681979c1f3d609614853b8cc6d3c761895fafcc200f2397</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:37:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-new-delhi-denies-claims-world-leaders-fell-ill-after-brics-summit/live-79300604--d5a9663f9e7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-new-delhi-denies-claims-world-leaders-fell-ill-after-brics-summit/live-79300604?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's foreign ministry rejected viral social media claims that leaders fell ill after the BRICS summit. Meanwhile, India defended its right to buy oil from diverse sources after the US passed a new sanctions bill.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How climate change worsened Nepal's deadly mountain collapse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb848ac0da373b91748348ad8b978bfd759e25f87f69d26ec151f735c634a7fd</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T23:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-worsened-nepal-s-deadly-mountain-collapse/a-79293578--691d9083ccec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-worsened-nepal-s-deadly-mountain-collapse/a-79293578?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A glacier and rock collapse in Nepal killed nearly 1,400 people and left thousands missing. Scientists say decades of warming helped set the disaster in motion.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>India news: US bill sanctioning Russia could hit India with tariffs of up to 100%</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac45d9d1c124d20b242e66289ab6e5a94ee8c2bc1b5d2a5bedce2150375db301</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T11:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-us-bill-sanctioning-russia-could-hit-india-with-tariffs-of-up-to-100/live-79285577--613ee224f2db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-us-bill-sanctioning-russia-could-hit-india-with-tariffs-of-up-to-100/live-79285577?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new bill could give President Trump the power to impose tariffs of up to 100% on countries buying Russian oil and gas, potentially affecting major importer India.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Duterte makes first appearance before ICC judges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93faa456b87dbf5fbad9fe76ae3f34ff7ff5548f278330429642849c59d13c9e</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/duterte-makes-first-appearance-before-icc-judges/a-79288207--0d857df202d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/duterte-makes-first-appearance-before-icc-judges/a-79288207?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte appeared in person at the ICC as judges considered claims of memory impairment and poor health. The 81-year-old is accused of crimes against humanity.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US allies in Asia alarmed as think tank calls for pullback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e81e74728d90b5faf9d2e9c033fa1baa88f47718da94b132984b2adc434080a</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554--5c1e9b8e70e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Analysts warn that a US withdrawal from the western Pacific, as recently suggested by a think tank, would weaken deterrence and strengthen China's position.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's 'Woman, Life, Freedom' spirit lives on amid war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:853fcaff81b8d4b87bdd560b80d93ab7ddc29d8f43c702cd34430a53a1fb50a6</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-woman-life-freedom-spirit-lives-on-amid-war/a-79276123--af9edc52c450.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-woman-life-freedom-spirit-lives-on-amid-war/a-79276123?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2022 death of Jina Mahsa Amini in police custody triggered a resistance movement in Iran. Four years later, the Iranian regime endures — but so does the legacy of the "Woman, Life, Freedom" protests.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Thousands still missing as flood recovery begins</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:196818ee9b6cfbfadfd7c8928232a0d38f03fc874f5666c8c40a1eaeaf16d8bd</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-flood-recovery-begins/a-79259980--8e8d61a072b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-thousands-still-missing-as-flood-recovery-begins/a-79259980?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Himalayan nation is moving from rescue operations to recovery, facing a $4.8 (€4.2) billion reconstruction bill amid renewed calls for climate justice.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pay to ghost your boss: Japan's resignation business</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04cc8565530b7122d68387ad5c4955c8a7902f7cabfaddbcc4cb995156d3aa55</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T10:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pay-to-ghost-your-boss-japan-s-resignation-business/a-79213584--1937a091cd92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pay-to-ghost-your-boss-japan-s-resignation-business/a-79213584?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Resignation agencies in Japan help employees leave their jobs seamlessly in just 15 minutes. Young people are especially eager to use their services.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why North Korea's Kim Jong Un doesn't need a US deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:541e08d52ed93cd30537d56f9ccb56fb8ccf447120d0621c9f926d140bc7e1f7</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854--e7f102464964.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-kim-jong-un-doesn-t-need-a-us-deal/a-79227854?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's overtures to North Korea's dictator have gone nowhere, with an emboldened Pyongyang accelerating its nuclear program and solidifying alliances with Russia and China.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Call in China to end English's core status sparks debate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17723f0e4d5d9acb58bf2b7cb5cd76525edef839001b72a779f58226a392d973</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/call-in-china-to-end-english-s-core-status-sparks-debate/a-79199629--c3ac5be694ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/call-in-china-to-end-english-s-core-status-sparks-debate/a-79199629?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A call to downgrade English in Chinese schools is fueling discussion over its value for students, careers and China's global competitiveness in the age of AI.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The billion-euro trade driving Europe's eels to extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63a01d78ddaa24d4f4d80db4d3fd33ad06cf9f4f95cdef512784b2e3c1b1fc65</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145--e574ad564b10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Traffickers are making big bucks smuggling millions of critically endangered eels across continents, using suitcases on planes and legal loopholes to deliver them to dinnerplates. Where are the smuggling hotspots?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Trafficked into fraud: An African crisis situation in Cambodia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bacfbbc8047ba53a96d798f79be5522bc4237f3356e13c84d0b1b37c42e07586</id><updated>2026-09-17T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967--d423991a2cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967?maca=en-rss-e